O.K. SPOILER, BLOW BY BLOW!!!

First of all, it DOES work. However, you must be standing close to the
drawbridge. I can't remember exactly which squares, but when you are
close enough you will know, because you will get the messages below.
Be careful too, won't you >;->.

When you play your instrument, and it askes "Improvise? (yn)" you must
answer NO.

Then you will be asked "What tune do you play (5 notes)?"
As we all know, musical notes go from A to G, so entering other letters
of the alphabet will not be very useful.

Entering five letters from A to G, you may then hear "gears turn" and
"tumblers click". For those that have never played Mastermind, one of
these means you have played a correct note, but in the wrong place. The
other means you have played the right note in the right spot. (I will
leave it to you to work out which is which). With some trail and error
and a bit of logic you can then work out what note goes where. When you
get all 5 notes in the right places, the drawbridge will drop.

